WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.010
Hi! How does a caterpillar become a butterfly? What does a baby cockroach look like? Today we'll look at insect life cycles.

2
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.370
A butterfly lays its eggs on leaves.

3
00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:21.090
A larva, the caterpillar, hatches from the egg. It eats leaves all the time and grows quickly.

4
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:27.738
The larva becomes a pupa. The pupa doesn't eat or move about, but it's changing inside.

5
00:00:27.888 --> 00:00:33.858
Finally, a butterfly comes out of the pupa, and it will lay eggs too.

6
00:00:34.008 --> 00:00:39.786
A mosquito also has four stages: egg, larva, pupa, adult.

7
00:00:39.936 --> 00:00:46.074
Mosquito larvae and pupae live in water, so don't leave water standing in flowerpots.

8
00:00:46.224 --> 00:00:52.770
A cockroach has only three stages: egg, nymph and adult. There's no pupa.

9
00:00:52.920 --> 00:01:01.002
A nymph looks like the adult, only smaller and without wings. Grasshoppers are like this too.

10
00:01:01.152 --> 00:01:05.418
Watch out! Not all insects have four stages!

11
00:01:05.568 --> 00:01:12.546
Cockroaches and grasshoppers have just three stages, egg, nymph and adult, with no pupa.

12
00:01:12.696 --> 00:01:18.162
Butterflies, mosquitoes and beetles have four stages.

13
00:01:18.312 --> 00:01:27.978
Your turn! Which stage of the butterfly's life cycle is a caterpillar? Pause and think.

14
00:01:28.128 --> 00:01:33.426
A caterpillar is the larva. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:33.576 --> 00:01:43.170
Another one! Which stage of a butterfly doesn't eat or move about? Pause and think.

16
00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:49.074
The pupa doesn't eat or move about. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:49.224 --> 00:01:58.458
Here's another! How many stages are in a cockroach's life cycle? Pause and think.

18
00:01:58.608 --> 00:02:04.578
Three: egg, nymph and adult. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:04.728 --> 00:02:13.818
Try one more! Why shouldn't water collect under flowerpots? Pause and think.

20
00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:22.674
Mosquito larvae and pupae live in water, so standing water lets mosquitoes breed. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:22.824 --> 00:02:31.914
Try one more! How is a cockroach nymph different from the adult? Pause and think.

22
00:02:32.064 --> 00:02:38.106
The nymph is smaller and has no wings. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:38.256 --> 00:02:46.218
Last one! Where do mosquito larvae live? Pause and think.

24
00:02:46.368 --> 00:02:52.866
Mosquito larvae and pupae both live in water. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:53.016 --> 00:03:04.866
Remember: butterflies and mosquitoes have four stages, egg, larva, pupa and adult. Cockroaches and grasshoppers have three, egg, nymph and adult.

26
00:03:05.016 --> 00:03:09.354
Check at home for any standing water!

